/target/
**/target/
.cxas/
.worktrees/
**/*.rs.bk
.superpowers/sdd/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
gauntlet/runs/

# Python virtual environments. A committed .venv is 400+ MB of platform-specific
# binaries that git can never forget, and that nobody can use on another OS.
.venv/
**/.venv/
venv/

# Demo-video render artifacts. All regenerable from scenes.py + narration.py:
# audio/ is ~95 MB of intermediate wavs, media/ is manim's partial-movie cache.
# The sources are worth keeping; the renders are worth rebuilding.
cxas-demo-video/audio/
cxas-demo-video/media/
cxas-demo-video/manim-mcp-server/src/media/

# Rendered demo videos and the vendored manim MCP server. The videos rebuild
# from scenes.py + narration.py; 18 MB of binary that git can never forget is a
# permanent cost for an artifact better attached to a release. The MCP server is
# a third-party copy with its own licence and belongs as a dependency.
cxas-demo-video/*.mp4
cxas-demo-video/manim-mcp-server/
